// Storm = a triggered ability that functions on the stack ([CR#702.40a]):
// "When you cast this spell, copy it for each other spell that was cast before
// it this turn. If the spell has any targets, you may choose new targets for
// any of the copies." An unparameterized composite-triggered keyword (like
// Mentor/Flying's `KeywordAbility(name, template, abilities)` form); multiple
// instances trigger separately ([CR#702.40b]), the engine's per-instance
// handling.
//
// Pieces (all over existing primitives):
//   - trigger:  `Cast(what: Ref(This))` — "when you cast this spell"
//               ([CR#601.2i]); the storm spell's own cast is the onset.
//   - count:    `EventCount(AllOf([Cast(who: Any, what: Any), Before(This)]),
//               ThisTurn)` — "each OTHER spell that was cast before it this
//               turn". `Before(This)` ([CR#702.40a]) keys on cast ORDER (log
//               position), so This's own cast (not before itself) drops out —
//               the "other" — and a spell cast in RESPONSE, a later cast the
//               turn tally still holds ([CR#603.3]), is excluded. This is why
//               a plain `EventCount(Cast, ThisTurn)` is wrong.
//   - effect:   `Repeat(<count>, CopySpell(controller: You, spec: (source:
//               Object(This)), retarget: AsIs))` ([CR#707.10]) — put that
//               many copies of the storm spell onto the stack.
//
// The reminder's "you may choose new targets for any of the copies" rider is
// OMITTED: it is a "may" ([CR#707.10c]) — `retarget: AsIs` keeps the
// original's targets, which is always legal — and `Repeat` binds no per-copy
// reference for a `MayChooseNew`/retarget rider to name. The copy count (the
// substantive storm behavior) is fully modeled.
KeywordAbility(
    name: "Storm",
    template: "storm",
    abilities: [Triggered(
        event: Cast(what: Ref(This)),
        effect: Repeat(
            EventCount(AllOf([Cast(who: Any, what: Any), Before(This)]), ThisTurn),
            CopySpell(controller: You, spec: (source: Object(This)), retarget: AsIs),
        ),
    )],
)
